# The re-created incarnation's first routing generation starts at 1, not at its
# initiator's routing floor plus one (#5668). Generation values recur, the #5641
# shape applied to generations. The live incarnation's own generation is at or
# below its floor, so the WAL refuses every claim it makes and #5705's guard fails
# its writes as deleted. Distinct from StraddlerBelowInitRoutingFloorAfterDeletes,
# which loses the floor itself (#5697 review, N1). Moved from the design's
# LiveGenerationAboveFloorRoutingRecreatedAtOne, re-anchored on the
# initialisation that seeds the generation.
MODULE: LiveGenerationAboveFloorRoutingRecreatedAtOne
TARGET: LiveGenerationAboveFloor
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: a re-created tree's first routing generation starts at 1, at or below its floor
PERTURBS: FirstInit

--- FIND
    /\ gen' = [gen EXCEPT !["s"] = rowFloor["s"] + 1]
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the first generation ignores the routing floor.
    /\ gen' = [gen EXCEPT !["s"] = 1]
--- END
